    {
      "id": "ff3192db-261b-4984-ac9b-f2f819813f8c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1440,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 688,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## Manage events in Google Calendar with an AI agent\n\nChat in plain language to add, move, delete and color-code Google Calendar events with your own categories.\n\n### Who's it for\nAnyone who wants to manage their calendar by chatting instead of clicking.\n\n### How it works\n1. You send a message in the chat, e.g. \"Add dentist tomorrow 3\u20134pm, category personal\".\n2. On the first message, the Categories data table is created automatically.\n3. A Gemini AI Agent reads your message, with today's date and your timezone added automatically.\n4. It finds, creates, moves, recolors or deletes events with the Google Calendar tools.\n5. Categories (name + color) live in the data table. The agent reuses a category, suggests a close match, or creates a new one with a free color.\n6. If details are missing, it asks instead of guessing.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Connect your Google Calendar OAuth2 credential in the calendar tools.\n2. Add your Google Gemini API key.\n3. Activate the workflow and click \"Open chat\".\n\n### Requirements\n- Google Calendar account\n- Google Gemini API key\n\n### How to customize\n- Swap Gemini for OpenAI or Anthropic.\n- Replace the chat trigger with Telegram or WhatsApp.\n- Edit the agent's system message to change its rules or tone."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
